++   "notes": "All 17 failing tests in packages/kernel/tests/value-diagnostic-work.test.ts are converted. The other 3 tests in the file (the UTF-16 preflight ones) are unchanged. The file passed 20/20 with node --test --experimental-strip-types on three consecutive runs, about 5 s each. `npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json` exited 0 for the whole repository. No other file was edited, and nothing under packages/kernel/src.\n\n**C1 ablation, run and verified.** Every mutant's `before` text was checked to occur exactly once in B (`git show b9c1e549:<path>`) and in the current file. Ablation ran in scratch copies, never in the shared tree:\n- B side: `git archive` of B's packages/kernel, with the original test file.\n- C side: a copy of the current packages/kernel, with the converted test file.\n- Both copies use a symlink to the repo's node_modules.\n\nFor each (test, mutant) pair, the mutant was applied, only that test was run (`--test-name-pattern` with the exact title), and the source was restored. Result: 43 pairs at B with the original tests and 43 pairs at C with the converted tests. All 86 were killed and none survived.\n- Mutant ids: MD1\u2013MD4, MD6\u2013MD8, MV1\u2013MV3, MB1\u2013MB2, MO1\u2013MO2, MC1, MR1.\n- MD8 (the catch label describes the container instead of the thrown value) does not kill the thrown-object deep-chain test at B or at C, because both labels are \"object\". It is claimed only for the thrown-null/arrays test, where it is killed.\n- Runner and results are in the session scratchpad, under tools/ (mutants.py, ablate.py) with ablation.log and ablation-results.json.\n\n**Instrument features implemented locally in the test file. capture-instruments.ts is untouched.**\n- A CHILD probe library (a string prepended to each `inWrappedChild` body):\n  - Per-target hook routing: Maps keyed by tracked object for descriptor, names, symbols and prototype, since the prelude exposes only one global hook per operation.\n  - `fixture`: the Proxy-free twin of the foreign / foreign-array / thrown-object fixtures.\n  - `rowFixture`: the twin of the decision-03/04 4,096-position rows. It counts prototypes, both listings, length descriptors and per-position descriptors, with an `unexpected` key counter.\n  - `deepAnswer`: hands the Kernel decision-03's prebuilt deep-prototype descriptors directly through the wrapped descriptor primordial.\n  - `disagreeingLength`: the length witness.\n  - The harness and assertOnlyRefusal, imported inside the child.\n- `tripwireFunction`: a plain function whose 13 diagnostic keys, own and inherited, are throwing counting getters.\n- `handlerFixture`: puts all 13 trap names behind counting getters at the end of the handler chain, so the witness proves no trap lookup, not just no trap call. `countingProxy` cannot express a deep handler chain.\n\n**Weakening disclosure (rule D).** An ordinary [[Get]] of own data on a plain object runs no caller code and cannot be wrapped. So the original `reads` and `lengthReads` counts cannot survive as counts. They are replaced by disagreement witnesses:\n- Read witness: the own descriptor says one value and the element holds another, so every read position is refused, and a skipped read would capture the descriptor's value instead.\n- Length witness: the own `length` descriptor says 4,095 while the read says 4,096.\n- In the byte-stop tests, the replacement is the meter's element units: 61,471, which pins the positions examined, each element unit being one descriptor plus one read.\n\nThese witnesses kill MV1 and MV2, which the original count assertions killed. All other counts stay exact, and the meter values were derived from the unit table and the shape before any run.\n\n**Proxy witnesses.** Each converted test keeps its original Proxy as a W witness, now refused with zero trap calls. That includes the eight-root Outcome and creation/ingress/recovery paths, with the same whole-state facts as before (classification, executionId null, position 0, retry position 1, assertOnlyRefusal, no deliveries).\n\n**Renames (rule D).** The six decision-03/04 tests now carry \"(item 5 superseded by decision-01 item 2)\". The unsupported-primitive test's meaning changed and it was renamed. Each renamed test quotes its original title in its one-line \"K1.1-correction-03: converted from \u2026\" comment, and every converted test has that comment.\n\nNo production change is needed.",
