++   "notes": "All 26 failing tests in packages/kernel/tests/values.test.ts are converted. The file now passes 84/84 with `node --test --experimental-strip-types`. `npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json` exited 0 with no errors anywhere when last run. I edited only values.test.ts; the other modified files in the checkout belong to concurrent agents. No production code, capture-instruments.ts, harness.ts or records were touched.\n\nC1 ablation:\n- Coverage: 48 (test, mutant) pairs across all 26 converted tests. Each mutant's at_b text occurs exactly once in `git show b9c1e549:packages/kernel/src/values.ts`, and each at_c text exactly once in the current values.ts (checked by script).\n- Method: ran in isolated `git archive` copies of B and HEAD under the scratchpad, never in the shared checkout. For every pair, the B copy with the at_b mutant ran the ORIGINAL test, and the C copy (HEAD plus my final values.test.ts) with the at_c mutant ran the CONVERTED test, each selected by `--test-name-pattern`.\n- Result: every mutant was KILLED on both sides, and all 52 unmutated baselines passed.\n- Every mutated values.ts still loads at B and at C, so no kill comes from a syntax error.\n- Every C-side kill is an assertion failure (`testCodeFailure`), not a crash or timeout. Two B-side kills (COST-array-structure-charge-dropped and COST-string-bytes-uncharged) happened through the original child's 60 s timeout, which the original test relied on. At C the same mutants are killed by exact issue and meter assertions (`too_much_work` instead of the byte stop).\n- Evidence is in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-arrokothi/277b30fa-4b8a-523f-b51a-f2df3201c4ce/scratchpad/mut/ (mutants.py, plan.py, ablate.py, results.json, ablate-final.log, reasons-C.json, syntax.py).\n\nMutants with shared before-text:\n- VAL-array-read-from-descriptor and VAL-object-read-from-descriptor share one at_b. B had a single read in describedValue; C splits it into observeElement and captureObject.\n- VAL-snapshot-is-cal