++   "notes": "All 10 failing tests in value-refusal-cost.test.ts are converted and every original title is kept. 33/33 tests pass under node --test --experimental-strip-types, and npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json reports no errors in the whole repository. Nothing under packages/kernel/src, capture-instruments.ts or any other test file was edited. There are no production change requests.\n\naggregate-refusal.test.ts passes 34/34 and is unchanged. It uses no Proxy. Its existing 17->18 code-count edit, with the comment that too_much_work and too_many_bytes are exclusive stops so one root still reports at most 11 value codes, matches values.ts: spend and charge both return early once state.stopped is set.\n\nC1 ablation method: 23 mutants, all run, none skipped.\n- B: a scratch extraction of b9c1e549 (git archive of package.json and packages/kernel, node_modules symlinked). Each at_b mutant was applied and the ORIGINAL test was run by exact title.\n- C: a scratch copy of the current packages/kernel (src identical to HEAD; HEAD moved to ebc6ae61 during the session, but src is unchanged since 01c01808). Each at_c mutant was applied and the CONVERTED test was run by exact title.\n- Every before string occurs exactly once at B and at C (checked by the runner).\n- Every mutant was killed at B by the original test and at C by the converted test.\n- The shared checkout was never mutated.\n- Tools and raw results are in the scratchpad:\n  - mutants.json, ablation-final.jsonl and ablation2.jsonl in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-arrokothi/277b30fa-4b8a-523f-b51a-f2df3201c4ce/scratchpad/\n  - mutants.py, ablate.py and gap.py in tools/ under that directory.\n\nOne instrument implemented locally (rule E): helperReadSites in value-refusal-cost.test.ts. It is a TypeScript-AST pin that the values.ts helper observeElement has exactly one container read site and no loop. It is needed because an ordinary own-data [[Get]] on a genuine array cannot be observed without a Proxy, and inWrappedChild cannot wrap it. Without the pin, RC-ELEMENT-READ-TWICE (a second read of each position, killed at B by reads===8*4096) survived the converted test; with it, the mutant is killed at C. If the lead prefers that pin in capture-metering.ts (a 'one read site per charged helper' rule), it can move there. This sits in design-01 \u00a71.5's declared gap 'extra work inside a helper', which the runtime oracle cannot see for [[Get]] either.\n\nTwo new tests (not conversions):\n- 'V-D1 every issue family: Proxy': ordinary, callable, array-target and revoked Proxies at 256 positions, with exact PROXY_MESSAGE details, suffix 248 and calls()===0 (decision-01 item 2).\n- 'V-D1 every issue family: re-prototyped built-in': a Map re-prototyped to Object.prototype at 256 positions, with exact BUILT_IN_MESSAGE details (decision-01 item 3 / design check Q4).\n\nEvery expected meter and tracked count was derived by hand from the unit table and the shape before the first run, and all matched on the first run. The derivations are in the comments next to each expectation.\n\nThe hook families run one wrapped child per test, about 0.2 s each; the file runs in about 2 s. The child-process timeout stays at the instrument default of 120 s. There are no timing gates.\n\nRule B: each W witness asserts the exact refusal (code, path and message, with suffix where positional) and calls()===0. The eager-roots witness also keeps the original whole-result facts: classification per arm, an exact reason with grant, no content without grant, assertOnlyRefusal and no delivery.",
