++   "notes": "I converted all 15 tests and validated them on Node v26.10.0. All four files pass (37, 34, 50 and 10 tests). `npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json` exited 0 with 0 errors overall when I ran it. I did not edit production code, capture-instruments.ts, harness.ts or any other file, and needed no production change. There are exactly 15 one-line markers starting `// K1.1-correction-03: converted from ... (authority)` (7 in creation, 5 in ingress, 2 in dispatch, 1 in outcome-hostile). Each renamed test keeps its identifier in the title and its original title in the comment.\n\nC1 ablation. Each mutant's before text occurs exactly once at B (`git show b9c1e549:<path>`) and once in the current file. The runner applied each mutant in a throwaway worktree and ran only the named test:\n- At B, the original tests killed every listed mutant.\n- At C, the converted tests killed every listed mutant, 30 of 30 test/mutant pairs.\n- Every kill at C comes from the converted mechanism, not the witness. Examples: child-probe assertions such as 'no exception escaped the creation boundary' and `payloadRefusal.ok` being true, same-call assertions such as 'the creation decision was actually retained' and 'no Kernel element reached the setter', and the freeze checks.\n- One mutant not claimed: V-KEYS-SLOT survived the original dispatch test at B, because that test never checked the bound identity. The converted dispatch test adds a replay assertion that does kill it at C. I report this as extra coverage, not as a C1 mutant.\n- Logs: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-arrokothi/277b30fa-4b8a-523f-b51a-f2df3201c4ce/scratchpad/ablation_b.txt and ablation_c_final.txt.\n- Mutant definitions and runner: scratchpad/tools/mutants_b.json, mutants_c.json, mutrun.py, plan.txt and plan_c.txt.\n- I removed the scratch worktrees afterwards; `git worktree list` is as I found it.\n\nSame-tick vector. I checked the order in coordinator.ts:\n- Creation observes scope, creationKey, the three revisions, authorityContext and the initialInput field. Then it captures authorityContext, then observes initialInput kind/payload/subscriptionClass, then captures payload, then commits.\n- Ingress observes destination, requestKey, kind, payload and subscriptionClass, then captures payload, then commits.\nSo an own `payload` getter on the input envelope runs inside the call, before the payload capture, serializer window and commit. An `authorityContext` getter on the request runs before any initial-input field is observed.\n\nThe getter installs the pollution before capture rather than mid-capture. For values.ts and the coordinator this is equivalent, because both use only load-time references and the window still runs after the pollution. Each converted test also keeps a countingProxy W witness: refused with the exact reason, `boundaryValueIssues` giving the Proxy message, `calls() === 0`, the side effect never installed, and nothing created or queued.\n\nChild probes. They inline a fake Driver, caller and request (CHILD_COORDINATOR in creation.test.ts; inline in ingress and outcome-hostile), because the child imports only the Kernel. No instrument extension was needed.\n\nNot converted: two tests in my files that pass on the Proxy refusal and no longer reach their mechanism. They were outside the 15 failing tests, so I left them; a follow-up may want to convert them:\n- creation.test.ts 'K11-R5-VAL-03 creation refuses a prototype observation that swaps the live Object binding' (getPrototypeOf-trap Proxy). Possible shape: an envelope getter swaps `globalThis.Object` to Fake, with payload = `Object.create(Fake.prototype)` carrying own a:1. A mutant comparing against the live `globalThis.Object.prototype` would then be killed.\n- dispatch.test.ts 'K11-R2-VAL-02 a payload with no single reading never reaches a Driver' (get-trap Proxy). It still asserts malformed_value and an empty driver.seen, but the disagreement check is no longer reached.\n\nThe revoked-Proxy identity-text tests (